    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">Paradoxes emerge not just in salons and ivory towers but in everyday life. (An Internet search for &quot;paradox&quot; brings forth a picture of an ashtray with a &quot;no smoking&quot; symbol inscribed on it.) Proposing solutions, Cuonzo writes, is a natural response to paradoxes. She invites us to rethink paradoxes by focusing on strategies for solving them, arguing that there is much to be learned from this, regardless of whether any of the more powerful paradoxes is even capable of solution.</marc:subfield>
